e.\n\nLet me think about known SMB1 area palette table. In the disassembly \"smbdis\", there's `AreaPalette` or `PaletteData`. Actually SMB uses `BG palette` table at $9C... Hmm. Let me recall: There's a table at $9C88? Not sure. Let's discover empirically.\n\nLet me first set up the hack and get to an area, read palettes. Let me start.\n\nLet me create hack first.\n\nThen for reaching areas, I'm on title screen (game_mode 0). The screenshot showed World 1-1 already (attract demo? Actually it showed a level with Mario). Wait the screenshot showed gameplay with WORLD 1-1. Hmm, status says RUNNING. It might be attract demo. The task says \"it is on its title screen or attract demo\". So need to reset to title.\n\nLet me be systematic. First create hack, use it. Then reset to title, then set bytes.\n\nActually, careful: writing $0760 etc. must happen on title screen before Start. Let me do reset_emulator, then verify title via screenshot.\n\nLet me begin.\n\nI'll load the persist-edit skill? The task involves proving a ROM edit with reset. The skill \"persist-edit\" seems relevant. Let me load it. Also maybe palette-swap. But the task is specific; I'll load persist-edit.\n\nActually the instructions say to load skills that match. persist-edit matches \"find where the bytes live in PRG ROM, write them there (ledgered), prove it with a reset, record the origin, and export a patch.\" This is exactly it. Let me load it.\n\nLet me do these in parallel: skill persist-edit, new_hack, reset_emulator? new_hack then use_hack. Let me call skill and new_hack together."}
