{"type":"thinking","text":"ROM byte is 0x2C (cyan) and the ledger edit is present. Yet palette RAM shows $27. So the palette is NOT loaded from 0xCEF for this area.\n\nSo the 16-byte match at 0xCEF is a different table. Hmm. But it exactly matches... Maybe that table is the palette source for areas selected by a *different* index, or it's used by the title/attract.\n\nLet me find the actual source. The reliable method: trace_writes on PPU palette address $3F00 (or $3F1D for palette 3 slot1) during level load. But trace_writes requires frames to run and refuses while paused. We need to trigger the palette copy.\n\nBetter: trace writes to PPU $3F1C-$3F1F (palette 3) while the level loads. We can reset, set area, start, and trace during the load. But trace_writes installs a callback for N frames and the game must perform the write during the window. We can do: reset, set area, then start trace_writes on ppu 0x3F00 length 32 for 300 frames, and during that window start the level via play_input? But trace_writes itself runs frames; does it accept input? No. Hmm.\n\nAlternative: trace_writes runs while the game is running; we can pre-arm it, then the game continues and loads the level. But we need to press Start during the trace window, and trace_writes doesn't take input. However the game is running during trace; if we start the trace right after pressing Start (i.e., at the level-load moment), the write happens during those frames.\n\nPlan: \n1. reset, write area, step.\n2. play_input [{start,8},{},30] — start the game; the card/level load will happen over next ~200 frames.\n3. Immediately call trace_writes on ppu 0x3F00 length 32 for 300 frames — but trace_writes will run 300 frames while the game continues, capturing the palette copy. Wait, does trace_writes run the game? Description: \"installs a callback on the range for N frames (default 60, max 600)\". It likely resumes the game for N frames. The game was paused at end of play_input; trace_writes \"Refused while paused (frames must run)\". So I need the game running. Hmm, trace_writes probably resumes.\n\nActually the ordering: after play_input the game is paused. Call trace_writes → it needs frames to run; maybe it resumes automatically? The description says \"Refused while paused\". So I should resume_emulator first, then trace_writes. But the palette copy happens at a specific time (level init), maybe within a few frames of the card ending. If I resume and immediately trace, good.\n\nBut timing: play_input [{start,8},{},30] → after ~38 frames we're just past Start; the game is in card/transition. Then resume and trace for 600 frames should capture the level-init palette write.\n\nEven simpler: trace the PPU palette during the whole sequence: \n- reset, write area, step.\n- resume_emulator\n- trace_writes address 0x3F00 length 32 mem_type ppu frames 600\nBut trace_writes runs 600 frames; during that, no Start is pressed. So the game stays on title.\n\nWe need Start. Hmm. Could we instead set the game to load the level without input? Not easily.\n\nAlternative: use trace_writes after initiating the start, and rely on the palette copy occurring a bit later. Let's estimate: from play_input, Start at frames 1-8, then mode 1. The level init/palette copy likely happens within ~30-60 frames after Start (during the card). In our runs, after start we saw card at +60 and level at +200. The palette copy might happen at the moment the level is initialized, maybe around frame ~150-200. So do play_input [{start,8},{},120] (ends ~128 frames, paused), then resume, then trace_writes for 300 frames. If the copy happens after frame 128, we catch it.\n\nActually, doing trace_writes requires not paused; I can call resume_emulator then trace_writes address 0x3F00 len 32 frames 400.\n\nBut there's risk the copy already happened before. Let me instead catch it at the earliest: after Start, the mode transitions. The palette copy for the area is likely part of level init which happens when the card