{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's what I found and proved.\n\n## How the game picks the palette\nThe area palette is one 32‑byte record in PRG ROM: 16 background palettes (4×4) then 16 sprite palettes. The records sit in a table of `[3F 00 20]` headers — PPU address `$3F00`, length 32 — each followed by 32 palette bytes and a `00` terminator, repeating every 36 bytes. `WriteVRAMBuffer` reads the record straight out of PRG and writes it to PPU `$3F00-$3F1F` at level load. A read trace on CPU `$8CEF` during a load caught exactly that: 32 reads from the copy loop at PC `$8EBE/$8EBB` (prgRom `0xEBB`).\n\nEach area was reached from the title screen by writing `$075C` (level digit), `$075F` (world) and `$0760` (area index), which the loader maps through `$9CB4`/`$9CBC` to the area header.\n\n## Results\n\n| Area | Area type / header | Palette table | Offset | Length |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **World 1‑2 underground** | type 2, header `$C0` | `0F 29 1A 09 … 0F 0C 3C 1C` | **prgRom 0xCEF** | **32** |\n| **World 2‑2 water** | type 0, header `$01` | `0F 15 12 25 … 0F 0F 30 10` | **prgRom 0xCA7** | **32** |\n| **World 1‑4 castle** | type 3, header `$60` | `0F 30 10 00 … 0F 00 30 10` | **prgRom 0xD13** | **32** |\n\n## Proofs (ledgered write → reset + `reapply_edits` → re‑enter area → undo)\n\n- **Underground:** wrote `0xCFC` (BG palette 3 slot 1) `$27`→`$2C`. Screenshot: the five `?` blocks and the HUD coin rendered **cyan** instead of orange; PPU `$3F0D` read `$2C`. Undone.\n- **Water:** wrote `0xCB1` (BG palette 2 slot 2, the water colour) `$12`→`$16`. Screenshot: the **entire sea turned red**; `get_pixel_color(128,100)` read `$16`, PPU palette 2 slot 2 read `$16`. Undone.\n- **Castle:** wrote `0xD18` (BG palette 1 slot 1, the brick colour) `$30`→`$16`. Screenshot: the **whole brick floor turned red**; a brick pixel read `$16`, PPU palette 1 slot 1 read `$16`. Undone. (A first try at `0xD14`, BG palette 0 slot 1, was invisible because the bricks use palette 1; it was undone.)\n\n## Bookkeeping\nEach was recorded with `record_mapping` (type `palette`, ids `underground` / `water` / `castle`, confidence 1, with `rom_origins`). `promote_mappings` was called (13 discoveries promoted). The throwaway hack `eval-sheet2-palettes` had every edit undone and its ledger is empty; the session is back on `use_hack default`."}
